      "writtenOn": "2025-01-22T22:06:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Paul. Thanks for the review!\n\nI did look at using the range_lock. The issue there is that that bow_write() (called from the workqueue) acquires the ranges_lock. That would result in a deadlock since state_store() need to hold that lock while flushing the workqueue.\n\n\nI think there are other alternative solutions to this problem, such as rewriting bow_write() to remove its assumption about the current state being CHECKPOINT, but believe the this current version of the change is easier to reason through. \n\nAlso, since we\u0027re not adding any additional mutex_lock() calls in the common (already committed path) and not meaningfully increasing lock contention even in the slow/workqueue path (since ranges lock already serializes work there) the performance impact of this change should be essentially nothing.",
      "parentUuid": "5585a18d_18d861f8",
      "revId": "0ee43711aad9fe3feecd0c15ec20935924b3066b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
